# OrbitAI Cleanup Issue List (Audit: 2026-03-30)


## 2) Legacy “glassy UI” compatibility layer still present
Files:
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/theme/Theme.kt` (lines ~281-373)
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/screens/ChatScreen.kt` (line ~1078 comment: `INPUT BAR — glassy floating bar`)
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/screens/SettingsSharedUi.kt` (`GlassCard` at lines ~126+)

Issue:
- Theme keeps a legacy glass system (`GlassTheme`, `LocalGlassTheme`) and gradient compatibility object (`OrbitGradients`) even though current design comments indicate a non-glass warm style.
- Naming + compatibility wrappers create confusing old-vs-new UI architecture.

## 3) Orphaned settings routes/screens (defined but not reachable from Settings UI)
Files:
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/navigation/NavGraph.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/screens/SettingsScreen.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/screens/SettingsInferenceScreen.kt`
- `app/src/main/java/com/example/orbitai/ui/screens/SettingsRagScreen.kt`

Evidence:
- Routes exist in `NavGraph.kt` (`settings/inference`, `settings/rag`, `settings/developer`) around lines 91-97 and composables around lines 264-287.
- `SettingsScreen.kt` only navigates to `settings/model`, `settings/memory`, `settings/tools`, `settings/orbit_bubble` (around lines 213, 218, 223, 237).

Impact:
- Dead/hidden UI paths and extra maintenance burden.



